# L §3.3: rate ± rate only "of one period"; comparisons "within one period".  A yearly and a monthly rate
# added are refused (LOAD-UNIT, "rate arithmetic outside §3.3"); the periods are in the values, so this is
# found when the values are read.  L §8.3: a load refusal means the model does not run, so it prints once,
# as a load refusal, not per value (the lead's note on writer 1's per-value LOAD codes).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
unit hour "godzina"

input a: rate
input b: rate

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 5 %/year
  b = 0.5 %/month

ask q1: a + b
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT ...
